<h2>Asobi 1.0 (build 1910) <span class="when">Oct 28, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Choosing online:</b> a link made for choosing now shows the layout you picked. Compare is a wipe the client drags across (or moves with the arrow keys), with a choice of what the first picture is set against; Grid shows each option as a card that opens all its pictures; Equal, Featured, Full page and Frames have their own arrangements.</li>
<li>The client can take a choice back: Choose again, or Clear choice.</li>
<li>Links made before this update keep the earlier layout: make a new link to send the new one.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<div class="earlier">Earlier updates</div>
<h3>1.0 (build 1904) <span class="when">Oct 28, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Presentations</b> (File ▸ Export ▸ Presentation…): put material in front of a client to decide on, as a PDF in the reports' design. A panel of five steps beside the document itself, drawn live.</li>
<li>Material from the playlist or a folder. Movies and sequences give their middle frame, start, middle and end (as one strip or separately), every Nth frame, or the frame on screen; a clip can have its own rule.</li>
<li>What is compared with what is yours: pictures start grouped by name, then make a new option from a selection, drag pictures between options, split, merge, take out, tick, rename, reorder.</li>
<li>Layouts: Featured, Equal, Grid, Full page, Frames and Compare. Any picture can also have a page of its own. Letter or A4, either orientation, a cover, captions, file names, dark pages, and room for the client's answer.</li>
<li><b>Choosing online:</b> Make a Link for Choosing puts the options on a web page where the client picks one and adds a note. The answer comes back to the panel, marked on the option.</li>
<li>The Contact Sheet window's PDF is now the Presentation panel.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1897) <span class="when">Oct 28, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Contact sheet as a PDF:</b> File ▸ Export ▸ Contact Sheet… can write design options as a PDF for a client, in the reports' design. Pictures whose names have the most in common make one option. A cover shows every option side by side, then each option has its page: its main picture large, its variants beside it, with captions you set once.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1894) <span class="when">Oct 28, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Fixed:</b> several folders dropped together added only the last one's pictures. They are now searched together, with one Cancel, and a new drop no longer stops one that is still being added.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1891) <span class="when">Oct 28, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Drop any folder:</b> Asobi searches it, and every folder inside it, for movies, image sequences and single pictures. A folder of stills used to be refused. When a picture is there as an EXR and a PNG, JPEG or TIFF, the display copy plays and the EXR is its source.</li>
<li><b>Cancel:</b> while a folder is searched and added, its progress shows with a Cancel button. Cancelling takes back what it added.</li>
<li>Progress and messages now sit under the title strip instead of at the foot of the picture, where the control bar covered them.</li>
<li><b>Fixed:</b> two different pictures in one folder no longer open as a two-frame sequence, and a folder dropped on the Playlist panel is no longer refused.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1888) <span class="when">Oct 28, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Compare with Plates in someone else's review:</b> a guest can now pair comps with their plates too. The plates are yours alone: they appear only in your playlist, and the wipe stays on your screen. You keep following the review, and see each comp against its plate whenever the review is on it. Before, a guest only got a note saying the host had to do it.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1885) <span class="when">Oct 28, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Fixed:</b> a live review with several Macs in it could get stuck re-sending the whole review to everyone several times a second. Playback stuttered, the picture jumped and menus wouldn't stay open. The host now brings newcomers up to date without setting that off. Hosts need this version; guests should update too.</li>
<li>Menus and the window no longer wait on the keychain each time they redraw.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1882) <span class="when">Oct 27, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Compare with Plates</b> (View ▸ Compare): every comp in the playlist against its shot's original plate, in a wipe, the plate under its comp. Clips from a Kitsu playlist take the plate movie from the shot's Plates task; clips from the shots folder take the plate's proxies, and zooming in shows the full-size plate. Right-click one comp for just that one.</li>
<li>The plate row's right-click menu switches plate (PL01, PL02…), fits the plate to the comp's width (on by default) and centers it. Drag the small up and down handle above the wipe's handle to move the plate under a repositioned comp. Everyone in the review sees the same framing.</li>
<li><b>Apply This Mode to All Pairs</b> (View ▸ Compare): every pair takes the mode on screen.</li>
<li><b>Fixed:</b> Macs that joined a review on the studio network couldn't play clips they had no file for, such as a Kitsu playlist's previews ("isn't on this machine"), while browsers could. They now stream the same review copies. The host needs this version too.</li>
<li><b>Fixed:</b> a paired Kitsu clip lost its pair when zooming in switched it to its source.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
